cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite the paper draft and this repository."
title: "The Catalogue Is the Instrument: how the choice of sign inventory moves the statistics of an undeciphered script (code and results)"
type: software
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-08-16"
authors:
  - family-names: "Väätäinen"
    given-names: "Ilpo"
    email: "ipezygj2@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ipezygj/rongorongo-catalogue-audit"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - rongorongo
  - undeciphered scripts
  - conditional entropy
  - transliteration
  - sign catalogue
  - Linear B
  - Rapa Nui
abstract: >
  Scripts and results measuring how much the choice of sign catalogue moves
  the length-normalised conditional entropy of the rongorongo corpus (CEIPP,
  25 objects), a sweep over catalogue sizes, composition tests against the
  scribes' own substitutions, syllabary references (Rapa Nui, Maori, Linear B)
  at matched size and length, and transliteration-noise and Miller-Madow
  checks. Standard-library Python; a fetch script downloads every input.
